# mipOS keeps ONLY these kernel drivers (modules), plus the drivers they need.
# Every other driver is deleted after each kernel install or update by
# /usr/local/sbin/mipos-trim-hardware (pacman hook 70-mipos-trim-hardware).
# Drivers built into the kernel itself (keyboard, battery, USB, NVMe/SATA,
# Btrfs, ext4...) always work and aren't listed here.
#
# Add a driver: put its name on a new line, then: sudo pacman -S linux
# A line with a "/" is a folder pattern (relative to the kernel's driver
# folder), e.g. crypto/* keeps every driver in kernel/crypto.
# Keep ALL drivers: put a line with only * , then: sudo pacman -S linux
# See /usr/share/mipos/HARDWARE.md.

